A||N||12||Bob Englert||NC Fiero owners get-together||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||11-15-2000||05:19 PM||||Fellow Fiero fans:<P>Thanks for all the input and responses to my question of interest in an<BR>informal Fiero get-together.<P>While there was interest expressed for both weekends (in Dec and Jan), there<BR>appears to be enough interest to plan for Saturday, Dec 16th at the Golden<BR>Corral steakhouse just off I-40 and Wendover Ave.  If we plan to meet about<BR>2:00 - 2:30 the lunch crowd should be thinned out some and will give time<BR>for owners from father away to come over.  There is ample parking at the<BR>Golden Corral and it is right next to Sams Club if we need a little more<BR>space.  Weather permitting, we can meet in the parking lot and get<BR>introduced and then go in together for a late lunch.  This should give<BR>owners from out of town plenty of time to get home afterward.  Anyone that<BR>can stay a while is welcome to stop by my house afterward.  (might put you<BR>to work though!).<P>Hopefully I will have the front suspension back in my blue 87 GT in time for<BR>the event.<P>If there is enough interest we might try to arrange a similar meeting in the<BR>Raleigh area in mid January.  Perhaps someone in Raleigh could suggest a<BR>location.  We can discuss further.<P>Some things to discuss:<BR>1) Is there any interest in a spring cruise through the mountains of NC, VA,<BR>or WV some weekend?<BR>2) Is there any interest in getting a group together to drive down to the<BR>swap meet at the Fiero Factory in Huntsville, AL the last weekend in April?<BR>Maybe going through Deal's Gap on the way!<BR>3)  Any interest in getting a group of cars to drive up to the national<BR>Fiero show being held in Williamsburg, VA in early August?<BR>4) How do we keep these cars healthy and on the road :-)<P>This is meant to be a relaxed, fun and informal way to meet other Fiero<BR>owners and discuss our common interest.  Please pass this along to any other<BR>Fiero owners or others interested in our favorite cars.<P>If you need directions once you get to Greensboro, my mobile phone # is<BR>(336) 707-9685.<P>I hope to meet many of you on Dec 16th...<P>Bob Englert<P><BR>Directions:<P>From east of Greensboro -<BR>1) I-40/I-85 west to split<BR>2) Take I-40 west (signs to Winston Salem) to exit 214 Wendover Ave.<BR>3) Left at top of exit onto Wendover Ave. West. Then get in right lane<BR>4) Right at first full traffic light at Marriot Courtyard hotel.<BR>5) Golden Corral is just to the left of the Cracker Barrel<P>From south of Greensboro -<BR>1) I-85 north to signs for I-40 west<BR>2) Take I-40 west (signs to Winston Salem) to exit 214 Wendover Ave.<BR>3) Left at top of exit onto Wendover Ave. West.  Then get in right lane<BR>4) Right at first full traffic light at Marriot Courtyard hotel.<BR>5) Golden Corral is just to the left of the Cracker Barrel<P>From west of Greensboro -<BR>1) I-40 east to first exit 214<BR>4) Stay to the right and take right at first full traffic light at Marriot<BR>Courtyard hotel.<BR>5) Golden Corral is just to the left of the Cracker Barrel<P><BR>||||reg||1
