Z||000005||LZeitgeist||12-17-2000||08:23 PM||||Hi, all - occasional lurker, first-time poster...<P>It was great meeting the NC folk - defintely looking forward to the next get-together. (Hopefully the weather will cooperate a bit more next time.)<P><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||12-17-2000||08:34 PM||||Want to say thanks to all that braved the weather and the traffic to meet for lunch.  Lyn, Megan, and I all had a great time.  Nice to see everyone.<P>Everyone seems to agree that we should do this again.  It was also agreed that we should take turns in different parts of the state to encourage more Fiero owners to join us.  I think it would make sense to try to met in the Raleigh area next time and maybe in Charlotte after that.  Hopefully we can connect with more of the SC Fiero owners in Charlotte.  I also want to see Bryan's killer Fieros!<P>Would January 20th work for most as a meeting date in Raleigh?  Check your schedules and let me know.<P>There was also interest in arranging some runs through the mountains in the spring and summer.  I look forward to setting some of these up.  IMO this is what a Fiero is meant to do!<P>Thanks again for all that took time to get together in Greensboro.<P>Happy holidays!<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroLisa||12-17-2000||08:55 PM||||Ya know I really might be in town that weekend- that's when I planned to bring the Fiero down...I Hope so!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
